-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 4: PERFORMANCE OF THE CONTRACT (ss 27 to 37).
-- The duties of ss 27, 28, 29(3), 32, 34 are also written as regulative rules in soga-duties; the
-- decision functions here are their asserted twins.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not
-- answer on these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

DECLARE `Place of delivery` IS ONE OF
    `the seller's place of business`
    `the seller's residence`
    `the place where the specific goods were, to the knowledge of the parties, when the contract was made`

DECLARE `Who is to move the goods` IS ONE OF
    `the buyer is to take possession of the goods`
    `the seller is to send the goods to the buyer`

DECLARE `Effect of a breach in an instalment contract` IS ONE OF
    `a repudiation of the whole contract`
    `a severable breach giving rise to a claim for compensation but not to a right to treat the whole contract as repudiated`
    `not yet resolved on the terms and circumstances`

DECLARE `Question material to a reasonable time` IS ONE OF
    `whether the buyer has had a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods for the purpose mentioned in subsection (2)`
    `some other question`

DECLARE `Reason for treating the buyer as not having accepted` IS ONE OF
    `he asks for, or agrees to, the repair of the goods by or under an arrangement with the seller`
    `the goods are delivered to another under a sub-sale or other disposition`
    `some other reason`

§ `Part 4 -- Performance of the contract`

§§ `Duties of seller and buyer (ss 27 and 28)`

-- s 27.  The seller's duty to deliver (twin of the regulative rule in soga-duties).
-- src:867 | 27. It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods, and of the buyer
-- src:868 | to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the
-- src:869 | contract of sale.
@ref s 27 seller (src:867-869)
GIVEN `the goods have been delivered in accordance with the terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27 the seller has performed his duty to deliver the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods have been delivered in accordance with the terms of the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods ... in accordance with the terms of the contract of sale" states the duty; it does not say what follows if the goods have not (yet) been delivered in accordance with the terms.
            NOTHING

-- s 27.  The buyer's duty to accept and pay (twin of the regulative rule in soga-duties).
-- src:867 | 27. It is the duty of the seller to deliver the goods, and of the buyer
-- src:868 | to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the
-- src:869 | contract of sale.
@ref s 27 buyer (src:867-869)
GIVEN `the buyer has accepted the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has paid for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27 the buyer has performed his duty to accept and pay for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer has accepted the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract` AND `the buyer has paid for the goods in accordance with the terms of the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the duty ... of the buyer to accept and pay for them, in accordance with the terms of the contract of sale" states the duty; it does not say what follows if the buyer has not done both.
            NOTHING

-- s 28.  Delivery and payment are concurrent conditions, unless otherwise agreed.
-- src:873 | 28. Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of
-- src:874 | the price are concurrent conditions, that is to say, the seller must be
-- src:875 | ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in
-- src:876 | exchange for the price and the buyer must be ready and willing to pay
-- src:877 | the price in exchange for possession of the goods.
@ref s 28 (src:873-877)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28 delivery of the goods and payment of the price are concurrent conditions` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of the price are concurrent conditions"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no when the parties have agreed otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:873 | 28. Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of
-- src:874 | the price are concurrent conditions, that is to say, the seller must be
-- src:875 | ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in
-- src:876 | exchange for the price and the buyer must be ready and willing to pay
-- src:877 | the price in exchange for possession of the goods.
@ref s 28 seller (src:873-877)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28 the seller must be ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in exchange for the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no when the parties have agreed otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:873 | 28. Unless otherwise agreed, delivery of the goods and payment of
-- src:874 | the price are concurrent conditions, that is to say, the seller must be
-- src:875 | ready and willing to give possession of the goods to the buyer in
-- src:876 | exchange for the price and the buyer must be ready and willing to pay
-- src:877 | the price in exchange for possession of the goods.
@ref s 28 buyer (src:873-877)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28 the buyer must be ready and willing to pay the price in exchange for possession of the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no when the parties have agreed otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Rules about delivery (s 29)`

-- s 29(1).  Whether the buyer takes possession or the seller sends is for the contract.
-- src:881 | 29.—(1) Whether it is for the buyer to take possession of the goods
-- src:882 | or for the seller to send them to the buyer is a question depending in
-- src:883 | each case on the contract, express or implied, between the parties.
@ref s 29(1) (src:881-883)
GIVEN `what the contract, express or implied, provides` IS A MAYBE `Who is to move the goods`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who is to move the goods`
DECIDE `s 29(1) whether the buyer is to take possession of the goods or the seller is to send them` IS
    CONSIDER `what the contract, express or implied, provides`
    WHEN JUST provided THEN JUST provided
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the question is "a question depending in each case on the contract, express or implied, between the parties", which is not among the sources.
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 29(2).  The place of delivery, apart from contract.
-- src:885 | (2) Apart from any such contract, express or implied, the place of
-- src:886 | delivery is the seller’s place of business if he has one, and if not, his
-- src:887 | residence; except that, if the contract is for the sale of specific goods,
-- src:888 | which to the knowledge of the parties when the contract is made are in
-- src:889 | some other place, then that place is the place of delivery.
@ref s 29(2) (src:885-889)
GIVEN `the contract, express or implied, fixes the place of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has a place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the knowledge of the parties when the contract was made the goods were in some other place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Place of delivery`
DECIDE `s 29(2) the place of delivery` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract, express or implied, fixes the place of delivery`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Apart from any such contract, express or implied" -- the contract decides the place.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contract is for the sale of specific goods` AND `to the knowledge of the parties when the contract was made the goods were in some other place`
        THEN JUST `the place where the specific goods were, to the knowledge of the parties, when the contract was made`
        IF `the seller has a place of business`
        THEN JUST `the seller's place of business`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the seller's residence`

-- s 29(3).  A seller bound to send the goods with no time fixed must send them within a reasonable time.
-- src:891 | (3) Where under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the
-- src:892 | goods to the buyer, but no time for sending them is fixed, the seller is
-- src:893 | bound to send them within a reasonable time.
@ref s 29(3) (src:891-893)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time for sending them is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(3) the seller is bound to send the goods within a reasonable time` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the goods to the buyer` AND (NOT `a time for sending them is fixed`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Where under the contract of sale the seller is bound to send the goods to the buyer, but no time for sending them is fixed". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 29(4), first limb.
-- src:895 | (4) Where the goods at the time of sale are in the possession of a
-- src:896 | third person, there is no delivery by seller to buyer unless and until the
-- src:897 | third person acknowledges to the buyer that he holds the goods on his
-- src:898 | behalf; but nothing in this section affects the operation of the issue or
-- src:899 | transfer of any document of title to goods.
@ref s 29(4) delivery (src:895-899)
GIVEN `at the time of sale the goods are in the possession of a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third person has acknowledged to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(4) there is delivery by the seller to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `at the time of sale the goods are in the possession of a third person` AND (NOT `the third person has acknowledged to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is no delivery by seller to buyer unless and until the third person acknowledges to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "unless and until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that there is no delivery until the third person acknowledges; once he does it does not say that there is delivery.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 29(4) there is delivery by the seller to the buyer`: the BAR as its own yes/no, "is delivery not yet possible?"
-- Ruled 2026-11-05 ("until" bars, fork F12): encode the bar and never claim that there is delivery.
-- JUST TRUE while the bar is in force (the goods were in the possession of a third person at the time of sale and he has not yet acknowledged to the buyer that he holds them on his behalf);
-- JUST FALSE once he has acknowledged, and JUST FALSE where the rule does not apply (no bar).
-- The acknowledgment is taken as of the time asked about, as in the function above, which is left as it was: JUST FALSE before it, NOTHING from it.
-- src:895 | (4) Where the goods at the time of sale are in the possession of a
-- src:896 | third person, there is no delivery by seller to buyer unless and until the
-- src:897 | third person acknowledges to the buyer that he holds the goods on his
-- src:898 | behalf; but nothing in this section affects the operation of the issue or
-- src:899 | transfer of any document of title to goods.
@ref s 29(4) bar (src:895-899)
GIVEN `at the time of sale the goods are in the possession of a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third person has acknowledged to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(4) delivery is not yet possible` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `at the time of sale the goods are in the possession of a third person`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the goods at the time of sale are in the possession of a third person"; otherwise there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the third person has acknowledged to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is no delivery by seller to buyer unless and until the third person acknowledges to the buyer that he holds the goods on his behalf" -- the bar lasts "until" then, so from then on it is not in force. This says nothing about whether there is delivery; that is the value of `s 29(4) there is delivery by the seller to the buyer`, NOTHING from the acknowledgment on. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (d): an "until" bar is its own yes/no function
            JUST FALSE

-- s 29(4), second limb.
-- src:895 | (4) Where the goods at the time of sale are in the possession of a
-- src:896 | third person, there is no delivery by seller to buyer unless and until the
-- src:897 | third person acknowledges to the buyer that he holds the goods on his
-- src:898 | behalf; but nothing in this section affects the operation of the issue or
-- src:899 | transfer of any document of title to goods.
@ref s 29(4) documents (src:895-899)
GIVEN `the question is the operation of the issue or transfer of a document of title to goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(4) section 29 affects the operation of the issue or transfer of a document of title to goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the question is the operation of the issue or transfer of a document of title to goods`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section affects the operation of the issue or transfer of any document of title to goods"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the clause speaks only of the issue or transfer of a document of title.
            NOTHING

-- s 29(5).  A demand or tender of delivery at an unreasonable hour may be treated as ineffectual.
-- src:904 | (5) Demand or tender of delivery may be treated as ineffectual
-- src:905 | unless made at a reasonable hour; and what is a reasonable hour is a
-- src:906 | question of fact.
@ref s 29(5) (src:904-906)
GIVEN `the demand or tender of delivery is made at a reasonable hour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(5) the demand or tender of delivery may be treated as ineffectual` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the demand or tender of delivery is made at a reasonable hour`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Demand or tender of delivery may be treated as ineffectual unless made at a reasonable hour"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless made at a reasonable hour" is read as the text's no when it is made at a reasonable hour.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 29(6).  Expenses of putting the goods into a deliverable state fall on the seller, unless otherwise agreed.
-- src:908 | (6) Unless otherwise agreed, the expenses of and incidental to
-- src:909 | putting the goods into a deliverable state must be borne by the seller.
@ref s 29(6) (src:908-909)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Party to the sale`
DECIDE `s 29(6) the party who must bear the expenses of putting the goods into a deliverable state` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise agreed"; the subsection does not say who bears the expenses under another agreement.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST Seller

§§ `Delivery of wrong quantity (s 30)`

-- s 30(1), first limb.
-- src:913 | 30.—(1) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods
-- src:914 | less than he contracted to sell, the buyer may reject them, but if the
-- src:915 | buyer accepts the goods so delivered, he must pay for them at the
-- src:916 | contract rate.
@ref s 30(1) reject (src:913-916)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1) the buyer may reject the goods delivered` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods less than he contracted to sell". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 30(1), second limb.
-- src:913 | 30.—(1) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods
-- src:914 | less than he contracted to sell, the buyer may reject them, but if the
-- src:915 | buyer accepts the goods so delivered, he must pay for them at the
-- src:916 | contract rate.
@ref s 30(1) pay (src:913-916)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer accepts the goods so delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the quantity delivered and accepted` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract rate per unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 30(1) the amount the buyer must pay for the goods delivered and accepted` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell` AND `the buyer accepts the goods so delivered`
        THEN JUST (`the quantity delivered and accepted` TIMES `the contract rate per unit`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty to pay at the contract rate arises "if the buyer accepts the goods so delivered" on a short delivery. The yes/no twin `s 30(1) the duty to pay at the contract rate for a short delivery that is accepted applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 30(1) the amount the buyer must pay for the goods delivered and accepted`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:913 | 30.—(1) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods
-- src:914 | less than he contracted to sell, the buyer may reject them, but if the
-- src:915 | buyer accepts the goods so delivered, he must pay for them at the
-- src:916 | contract rate.
@ref s 30(1) pay applies (src:913-916)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer accepts the goods so delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1) the duty to pay at the contract rate for a short delivery that is accepted applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is less than the seller contracted to sell` AND `the buyer accepts the goods so delivered`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the buyer accepts the goods so delivered, he must pay for them at the contract rate" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 30(2).
-- src:918 | (2) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger
-- src:919 | than he contracted to sell, the buyer may accept the goods included in
-- src:920 | the contract and reject the rest, or he may reject the whole.
@ref s 30(2) accept (src:918-920)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2) the buyer may accept the goods included in the contract and reject the rest` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger than he contracted to sell". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:918 | (2) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger
-- src:919 | than he contracted to sell, the buyer may accept the goods included in
-- src:920 | the contract and reject the rest, or he may reject the whole.
@ref s 30(2) whole (src:918-920)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2) the buyer may reject the whole` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger than he contracted to sell". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 30(2A).  A buyer who does not deal as consumer may not reject for a slight shortfall or excess.
-- src:922 | (2A) A buyer who does not deal as consumer may not —
-- src:924 | (a) where the seller delivers a quantity of goods less than he
-- src:925 | contracted to sell, reject the goods under subsection (1); or
-- src:927 | (b) where the seller delivers a quantity of goods larger than he
-- src:928 | contracted to sell, reject the whole under subsection (2),
-- src:930 | if the shortfall or, as the case may be, excess is so slight that it would
-- src:931 | be unreasonable for the buyer to do so.
@ref s 30(2A) (src:922-931)
GIVEN `the buyer deals as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shortfall or excess is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to reject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2A) the buyer may reject the goods under subsection (1) or reject the whole under subsection (2)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the buyer deals as consumer`) AND `the shortfall or excess is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to reject`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A buyer who does not deal as consumer may not ... reject the goods under subsection (1) ... reject the whole under subsection (2), if the shortfall or, as the case may be, excess is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to do so."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition covers only "A buyer who does not deal as consumer" and a shortfall or excess "so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to do so".
            NOTHING

-- s 30(2B).  The burden is on the seller.
-- src:935 | (2B) It is for the seller to show that a shortfall or excess fell within
-- src:936 | subsection (2A).
@ref s 30(2B) (src:935-936)
GIVEN `the seller has shown that the shortfall or excess fell within subsection (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2B) the shortfall or excess is treated as one that fell within subsection (2A)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller has shown that the shortfall or excess fell within subsection (2A)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is for the seller to show that a shortfall or excess fell within subsection (2A)."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a burden rule is read as the text's no when the seller has not shown it; the other reading is that the text says only who must show.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 30(3).
-- src:938 | (3) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger
-- src:939 | than he contracted to sell and the buyer accepts the whole of the goods
-- src:940 | so delivered, he must pay for them at the contract rate.
@ref s 30(3) (src:938-940)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole quantity delivered` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract rate per unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 30(3) the amount the buyer must pay for the whole of the goods delivered and accepted` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` AND `the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered`
        THEN JUST (`the whole quantity delivered` TIMES `the contract rate per unit`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises "Where the seller delivers ... a quantity of goods larger than he contracted to sell and the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered". The yes/no twin `s 30(3) the duty to pay at the contract rate for the whole of an excess that is accepted applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 30(3) the amount the buyer must pay for the whole of the goods delivered and accepted`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:938 | (3) Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger
-- src:939 | than he contracted to sell and the buyer accepts the whole of the goods
-- src:940 | so delivered, he must pay for them at the contract rate.
@ref s 30(3) applies (src:938-940)
GIVEN `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(3) the duty to pay at the contract rate for the whole of an excess that is accepted applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity delivered is larger than the seller contracted to sell` AND `the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the seller delivers to the buyer a quantity of goods larger than he contracted to sell and the buyer accepts the whole of the goods so delivered he must pay for them at the contract rate" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 30(4).
-- src:942 | (4) This section is subject to any usage of trade, special agreement,
-- src:943 | or course of dealing between the parties.
@ref s 30(4) (src:942-943)
GIVEN `there is a usage of trade, special agreement or course of dealing between the parties that displaces section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(4) section 30 gives way to a usage of trade, special agreement or course of dealing` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a usage of trade, special agreement or course of dealing between the parties that displaces section 30`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section is subject to any usage of trade, special agreement, or course of dealing between the parties"; where there is none the subsection is silent.
            NOTHING

§§ `Instalment deliveries (s 31)`

-- s 31(1).
-- src:947 | 31.—(1) Unless otherwise agreed, the buyer of goods is not bound
-- src:948 | to accept delivery of them by instalments.
@ref s 31(1) (src:947-948)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(1) the buyer is bound to accept delivery of the goods by instalments` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise agreed"; the subsection says nothing under another agreement.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed, the buyer of goods is not bound to accept delivery of them by instalments."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no; the other reading is that "Unless otherwise agreed" states an exception only and the text is silent when it fails.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 31(2).
-- src:953 | (2) Where there is a contract for the sale of goods to be delivered by
-- src:954 | stated instalments, which are to be separately paid for, and the seller
-- src:955 | makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or
-- src:956 | the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more
-- src:957 | instalments, it is a question in each case depending on the terms of the
-- src:958 | contract and the circumstances of the case whether the breach of
-- src:959 | contract is a repudiation of the whole contract or whether it is a
-- src:960 | severable breach giving rise to a claim for compensation but not to a
-- src:961 | right to treat the whole contract as repudiated.
@ref s 31(2) (src:953-961)
GIVEN `the contract is for goods to be delivered by stated instalments which are to be separately paid for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the terms of the contract and the circumstances of the case make of the breach` IS A `Effect of a breach in an instalment contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Effect of a breach in an instalment contract`
DECIDE `s 31(2) the breach of contract is a repudiation of the whole contract or a severable breach` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the contract is for goods to be delivered by stated instalments which are to be separately paid for` AND `the seller makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more instalments`)
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of goods to be delivered by stated instalments, which are to be separately paid for" and one of the named breaches occurs. The yes/no twin `s 31(2) the question of repudiation or severable breach arises` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING
        IF `what the terms of the contract and the circumstances of the case make of the breach` EQUALS `not yet resolved on the terms and circumstances`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "it is a question in each case depending on the terms of the contract and the circumstances of the case".
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST `what the terms of the contract and the circumstances of the case make of the breach`

-- Twin of `s 31(2) the breach of contract is a repudiation of the whole contract or a severable breach`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:953 | (2) Where there is a contract for the sale of goods to be delivered by
-- src:954 | stated instalments, which are to be separately paid for, and the seller
-- src:955 | makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or
-- src:956 | the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more
-- src:957 | instalments, it is a question in each case depending on the terms of the
-- src:958 | contract and the circumstances of the case whether the breach of
-- src:959 | contract is a repudiation of the whole contract or whether it is a
-- src:960 | severable breach giving rise to a claim for compensation but not to a
-- src:961 | right to treat the whole contract as repudiated.
@ref s 31(2) applies (src:953-961)
GIVEN `the contract is for goods to be delivered by stated instalments which are to be separately paid for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(2) the question of repudiation or severable breach arises` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is for goods to be delivered by stated instalments which are to be separately paid for` AND `the seller makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more instalments`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a contract for the sale of goods to be delivered by stated instalments, which are to be separately paid for, and the seller makes defective deliveries in respect of one or more instalments, or the buyer neglects or refuses to take delivery of or pay for one or more instalments" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Delivery to carrier and risk in transit (ss 32 and 33)`

-- s 32(1).
-- src:965 | 32.—(1) Where, in pursuance of a contract of sale, the seller is
-- src:966 | authorised or required to send the goods to the buyer, delivery of the
-- src:967 | goods to a carrier (whether named by the buyer or not) for the purpose
-- src:968 | of transmission to the buyer is prima facie deemed to be a delivery of
-- src:969 | the goods to the buyer.
@ref s 32(1) (src:965-969)
GIVEN `in pursuance of the contract of sale the seller is authorised or required to send the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller delivers the goods to a carrier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(1) delivery of the goods to the carrier is deemed to be a delivery of the goods to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`in pursuance of the contract of sale the seller is authorised or required to send the goods to the buyer` AND `the seller delivers the goods to a carrier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where, in pursuance of a contract of sale, the seller is authorised or required to send the goods to the buyer" and delivers them to a carrier for transmission. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prima facie" -- the deeming yields to proof of the contrary.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 32(2), first limb: the seller's duty.
-- src:971 | (2) Unless otherwise authorised by the buyer, the seller must make
-- src:972 | such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be
-- src:973 | reasonable having regard to the nature of the goods and the other
-- src:974 | circumstances of the case; and if the seller omits to do so, and the
-- src:975 | goods are lost or damaged in course of transit, the buyer may decline
-- src:976 | to treat the delivery to the carrier as a delivery to himself or may hold
-- src:977 | the seller responsible in damages.
@ref s 32(2) duty (src:971-977)
GIVEN `the buyer has otherwise authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(2) the seller must make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer has otherwise authorised`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise authorised by the buyer, the seller must make such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be reasonable"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise authorised by the buyer" is read as the text's no when the buyer has authorised otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 32(2), second limb: the buyer's remedies.
-- src:971 | (2) Unless otherwise authorised by the buyer, the seller must make
-- src:972 | such contract with the carrier on behalf of the buyer as may be
-- src:973 | reasonable having regard to the nature of the goods and the other
-- src:974 | circumstances of the case; and if the seller omits to do so, and the
-- src:975 | goods are lost or damaged in course of transit, the buyer may decline
-- src:976 | to treat the delivery to the carrier as a delivery to himself or may hold
-- src:977 | the seller responsible in damages.
@ref s 32(2) remedies (src:971-977)
GIVEN `the seller omitted to make a reasonable contract with the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are lost or damaged in course of transit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(2) the buyer may decline to treat the delivery to the carrier as a delivery to himself or hold the seller responsible in damages` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller omitted to make a reasonable contract with the carrier` AND `the goods are lost or damaged in course of transit`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the remedies arise "if the seller omits to do so, and the goods are lost or damaged in course of transit". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 32(3).
