      `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is usual to insure in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(3) the seller must give the buyer such notice as may enable him to insure the goods during their sea transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no when the parties have agreed otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` AND `it is usual to insure in the circumstances`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "where goods are sent by the seller to the buyer by a route involving sea transit, under circumstances in which it is usual to insure". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:979 | (3) Unless otherwise agreed, where goods are sent by the seller to
-- src:980 | the buyer by a route involving sea transit, under circumstances in
-- src:981 | which it is usual to insure, the seller must give such notice to the
-- src:982 | buyer as may enable him to insure them during their sea transit; and if
-- src:983 | the seller fails to do so, the goods are at his risk during such sea
-- src:984 | transit.
