      `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is usual to insure in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller fails to give the buyer notice enabling him to insure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(3) the goods are at the seller's risk during the sea transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise agreed"; the subsection says nothing under another agreement.
            NOTHING
        IF `the goods are sent by a route involving sea transit` AND `it is usual to insure in the circumstances` AND `the seller fails to give the buyer notice enabling him to insure`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
