§§ `The buyer's right of examining, and acceptance (ss 34 to 37)`

-- s 34.
-- src:998 | 34. Unless otherwise agreed, when the seller tenders delivery of the
-- src:999 | goods to the buyer, he is bound on request to afford the buyer a
-- src:1000 | reasonable opportunity of examining the goods for the purpose of
-- src:1001 | ascertaining whether they are in conformity with the contract and, in
-- src:1002 | the case of a contract for sale by sample, of comparing the bulk with
-- src:1003 | the sample.
@ref s 34 (src:998-1003)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller tenders delivery of the goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer requests an opportunity of examining the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 34 the seller is bound to afford the buyer a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise agreed"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless otherwise agreed" is read as the text's no when the parties have agreed otherwise.
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the seller tenders delivery of the goods to the buyer` AND `the buyer requests an opportunity of examining the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "when the seller tenders delivery of the goods to the buyer" and is "bound on request". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 35(1).  The two ways of acceptance in subsection (1).
-- src:1007 | 35.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), the buyer is deemed to have
-- src:1008 | accepted the goods —
-- src:1010 | (a) when he intimates to the seller that he has accepted them;
-- src:1011 | or
-- src:1013 | (b) when the goods have been delivered to him and he does
-- src:1014 | any act in relation to them which is inconsistent with the
-- src:1015 | ownership of the seller.
@ref s 35(1) (src:1007-1015)
GIVEN `the buyer intimates to the seller that he has accepted the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods have been delivered to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer does an act in relation to the goods which is inconsistent with the ownership of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(1) the buyer is deemed to have accepted the goods under subsection (1)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer intimates to the seller that he has accepted the goods` OR (`the goods have been delivered to the buyer` AND `the buyer does an act in relation to the goods which is inconsistent with the ownership of the seller`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (1) names two occasions and does not say that the buyer is deemed not to have accepted on any other; ss 35(4) and (7) add others.
            NOTHING

-- s 35(2).  No acceptance under (1) before a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods.
-- src:1017 | (2) Where goods are delivered to the buyer and he has not
-- src:1018 | previously examined them, he is not deemed to have accepted
-- src:1019 | them under subsection (1) until he has had a reasonable opportunity
-- src:1020 | of examining them for the purpose —
-- src:1022 | (a) of ascertaining whether they are in conformity with the
-- src:1023 | contract; and
-- src:1025 | (b) in the case of a contract for sale by sample, of comparing
-- src:1026 | the bulk with the sample.
@ref s 35(2) (src:1017-1026)
GIVEN `goods are delivered to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has previously examined them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has had a reasonable opportunity of examining them for the purposes in paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(2) the buyer is deemed to have accepted the goods under subsection (1)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `goods are delivered to the buyer` AND (NOT `he has previously examined them`) AND (NOT `he has had a reasonable opportunity of examining them for the purposes in paragraphs (a) and (b)`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he is not deemed to have accepted them under subsection (1) until he has had a reasonable opportunity of examining them"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of goods delivered that the buyer "has not previously examined", and only of the time before the reasonable opportunity.
            NOTHING

-- s 35(3).
-- src:1028 | (3) Where the buyer deals as consumer, the buyer cannot lose his
-- src:1029 | right to rely on subsection (2) by agreement, waiver or otherwise.
@ref s 35(3) (src:1028-1029)
GIVEN `the buyer deals as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(3) the buyer can lose his right to rely on subsection (2) by agreement, waiver or otherwise` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer deals as consumer`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the buyer deals as consumer, the buyer cannot lose his right to rely on subsection (2) by agreement, waiver or otherwise."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where the buyer deals as consumer".
            NOTHING

-- s 35(4).
-- src:1031 | (4) The buyer is also deemed to have accepted the goods when after
-- src:1032 | the lapse of a reasonable time he retains the goods without intimating
-- src:1033 | to the seller that he has rejected them.
@ref s 35(4) (src:1031-1033)
GIVEN `a reasonable time has lapsed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer retains the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has intimated to the seller that he has rejected them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(4) the buyer is deemed to have accepted the goods after a reasonable time` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a reasonable time has lapsed` AND `the buyer retains the goods` AND (NOT `the buyer has intimated to the seller that he has rejected them`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection says the buyer is deemed to have accepted "when after the lapse of a reasonable time he retains the goods without intimating to the seller that he has rejected them". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 35(5).
-- src:1035 | (5) The questions that are material in determining for the purposes
-- src:1036 | of subsection (4) whether a reasonable time has elapsed include
-- src:1037 | whether the buyer has had a reasonable opportunity of examining the
-- src:1038 | goods for the purpose mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 35(5) (src:1035-1038)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `Question material to a reasonable time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(5) the question is material in determining whether a reasonable time has elapsed for the purposes of subsection (4)` IS
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `whether the buyer has had a reasonable opportunity of examining the goods for the purpose mentioned in subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The questions that are material ... include ..." -- the list is not closed.
    WHEN `some other question` THEN NOTHING

-- s 35(6).
-- src:1043 | (6) The buyer is not by virtue of this section deemed to have
-- src:1044 | accepted the goods merely because —
-- src:1046 | (a) he asks for, or agrees to, their repair by or under an
-- src:1047 | arrangement with the seller; or
-- src:1049 | (b) the goods are delivered to another under a sub-sale or other
-- src:1050 | disposition.
@ref s 35(6) (src:1043-1050)
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for treating the buyer as not having accepted`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(6) the buyer is deemed to have accepted the goods by virtue of section 35 merely because of the reason` IS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The buyer is not by virtue of this section deemed to have accepted the goods merely because (a) he asks for, or agrees to, their repair by or under an arrangement with the seller"
    WHEN `he asks for, or agrees to, the repair of the goods by or under an arrangement with the seller` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The buyer is not by virtue of this section deemed to have accepted the goods merely because ... (b) the goods are delivered to another under a sub-sale or other disposition."
    WHEN `the goods are delivered to another under a sub-sale or other disposition` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two reasons.
    WHEN `some other reason` THEN NOTHING

