        IF `s 35(7) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 35(2) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he is not deemed to have accepted them under subsection (1) until he has had a reasonable opportunity of examining them" (s 35(2)); no other route (s 35(4), (7)) applies.
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        IF `s 35(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no route in s 35 applies on these facts.
            NOTHING

-- s 35A(1).
